  "id": "COMPOUND:28839 - PROTEIN:1507",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (5S,6R)-10,12-dihydroxy-5-methyl-6-(3-oxobut-1-en-2-yl)-11-propan-2-yl-2-oxatricyclo[7.3.1.05,13]trideca-1(12),9(13),10-triene-3,8-dione, is shown to interact with Cytochrome P450 1A2 through multiple pathways. It is a target of three different compounds: 2,5-Dimethyl-1,6-heptadiene, Berkeleyacetal B, and (2R)-7,4'-Dihydroxy-5-Methoxy-8-Methylflavan. These compounds are all linked to the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha, which in turn is a target of the compound in question. This suggests a potential mechanism where the compound may influence the activity of the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha, which then affects Cytochrome P450 1A2. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a possible role for the compound in modulating the expression or activity of Cytochrome P450 1A2. The relationship is supported by multiple independent targets, suggesting a robust biological connection. However, the exact mechanism by which the compound interacts with Cytochrome P450 1A2 remains to be fully elucidated.",
